-- title:
--   At a crossing, primes over p are the two branch primes
-- statement:
--   Let $p\ge 5$ be a prime and let $\mathfrak X$ be a `DRModelPackage p`, i.e. a bundle of data and properties for the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` of the modular curve over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z$ (properness, flatness and integrality of `DRModel.toBase p`, integral closedness of the sections over affine opens, models of the generic fibre over $\mathbb Q$ and over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with their Galois and place compatibilities, two sections of the structure map, a distinguished smooth locus, and further data). Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, and assume the base change $\mathfrak X_O := \mathrm{DRModel}\,p \times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z}\operatorname{Spec}O$ is an integral scheme. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, let $\mathrm{to}\kappa\colon O\to k$ be a ring homomorphism, and let $x$ be a point of $\mathfrak X_O$ whose local ring $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X_O,x}$ is Noetherian. Assume that the generic point of the curve $(\mathfrak X.\mathrm{ratModel}\,k).C$, pushed forward along each of the two morphisms $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,k$ and $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\,k$ followed by the base-change map `DRModel.baseChangeMap` $\mathrm{to}\kappa$, specialises to $x$; call these hypotheses $h_1$ and $h_2$. Write $\mathfrak p_i\subset\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X_O,x}$ for the preimage of the maximal ideal of the stalk at that generic point under the specialisation map of $h_i$. Then $\mathfrak p_1$ and $\mathfrak p_2$ are prime, both contain $p$, every prime of $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X_O,x}$ minimal over the ideal $(p)$ equals $\mathfrak p_1$ or $\mathfrak p_2$, and every prime of height $1$ containing $p$ equals $\mathfrak p_1$ or $\mathfrak p_2$.
--
--   This is the local statement at a crossing point of the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model: the two labelled components through $x$ account for all primes of the local ring minimal over $(p)$, equivalently (by Krull's Hauptidealsatz in the Noetherian local ring) all height-one primes containing $p$. It is used in the identification of the intersection of the two branch ideals at such a point with the ideal generated by the germ of $p$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_DRModelPackage_eq_comap_or_eq_comap_of_mem_minimalPrimes_natCast_of_specializes.lean

